ne Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "85ab1464-6c15-5893-8d56-cce6e3650dca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251672} {:answer/id #uuid "8b420990-483b-572d-8a5a-8a20fa791603" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{10}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251729} {:answer/id #uuid "912723c2-81e8-5e56-a4a7-64e4a72dd73f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{e}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251791} {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac8965-5a85-5f71-b2f3-7263eb99c325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252097} {:answer/id #uuid "b2969f44-59d5-5d35-86cd-28c526b1fe59" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\sqrt{6}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252114}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b0ac8965-5a85-5f71-b2f3-7263eb99c325" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{7}{10}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252097} :answer-field/id #uuid "cb546713-1424-5afe-bb7a-e435d235d0d0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253154}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "084a7b4b-8361-5ab7-b547-58636a48752e" :question/math-academy-id "q-116966" :question/problem "Which of the following values is in the domain of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's recall the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n![](images/df/df22eea4331c47da3047381ca672fd80ebf75118054316fe88c0e2d96dae0d34.png)\n\nNote that:\n\n- The domain of the function is $x\\in [-1,1].$\n\nTherefore, of the given values, only $x=-\\frac{7}{10}$ is in the domain of the function."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399926 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110571 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "67692569-e3a4-51e8-99ac-79d8b3081363" :knowledge-point/title "Determining Points that Lie on the Curve of the Inverse Sine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c97697d4-12b3-5718-85d8-ccf9baa9c0b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399928} {:answer/id #uuid "89b62b05-1225-5e0f-aaa9-52691a529d7c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I and III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399929} {:answer/id #uuid "14432c27-d6ae-50d5-8dba-d5691721386e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "I only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399930} {:answer/id #uuid "090ba0b9-9a7f-56da-a9e2-3c7744cb2594" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "III only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399931} {:answer/id #uuid "1e1d97c2-6d62-5f88-b357-30e7e1bfcc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399932}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1e1d97c2-6d62-5f88-b357-30e7e1bfcc80" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "II only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399932} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a03d965-da67-51fe-9c15-60bc125eaf3d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399927}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8d72740e-6072-5046-bfdb-c5667ec877d5" :question/math-academy-id "q-117012" :question/problem "Which of the following points lies on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x?$\n\nI. $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$\nII. $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$\nIII. $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{4})$" :question/worked-solution "In order for a point $(a,b)$ to lie on the graph of the function $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ the following conditions must hold:\n\n- The reflected point $(b,a)$ must lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x,$ meaning $a=\\operatorname{sin}⁡b.$\n\n- The $y$-value of the point must lie in the range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x,$ which is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}].$\n\nWith this in mind, let's check each of the points. \n\n- First, we consider the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.$  $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(\\frac{\\pi }{4},\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Next, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(-\\frac{\\pi }{3},-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=-\\frac{\\pi }{3}$ lies within this range. $\\,✓$\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{2},-\\frac{\\pi }{3})$ does lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$\n\n- Finally, we consider the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{4}).$ We note the following:\n\n- The point $(\\frac{5\\pi }{4},-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2})$ lies on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡x.\\,✓$\n\n- The range of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x$ is $y\\in [-\\frac{\\pi }{2},\\frac{\\pi }{2}],$ and $y=\\frac{5\\pi }{4}$ does **not** lie within this range. $\\,\\times $\n\nTherefore, the point $(-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2},\\frac{5\\pi }{4})$ does **not** lie on the graph of $y=\\operatorname{arcsin}⁡x.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253302 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087655 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "82d6988b-3220-578f-ba1c-cd86b9e3dbf9" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and the Radius"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2b15e7a5-78ca-5688-a932-a2ff47f3474b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250921} {:answer/id #uuid "303b72ca-c041-5f4d-ba88-cfc9252584e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250963} {:answer/id #uuid "58063976-49ff-516f-bbee-085c50f0cd83" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251273} {:answer/id #uuid "730971b8-62e4-54a4-a7ef-c3267c982997" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=7" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251502} {:answer/id #uuid "cc0cfc11-8f30-57fc-b4eb-7dbd668540da" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252356}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "303b72ca-c041-5f4d-ba88-cfc9252584e0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2}=49" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250963} :answer-field/id #uuid "e8df55f5-2f9b-5f02-9b2c-4736a5b8b86a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253211}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5dd64115-dbeb-5cf8-8fc0-3bacf50a0c2c" :question/math-academy-id "q-117081" :question/problem "![](images/98/9839540667b095cec69ce6ea429aa99b129e90fee26c4adf1f25ffa6019d5067.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the circle given above?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nFrom the picture, we see that our circle is centered at $C(-5,0)$ and the radius of the circle is $r=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the circle is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ {(x-(-5))}^{2}+(y-0)^{2} & ={7}^{2} \\\\ (x+5)^{2}+{y}^{2} & =49.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186399940 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087656 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "89462485-2e28-5727-82c7-7afd0cac6d77" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Center and Radius of a Circle Given Its Equation"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e41033f-736e-5607-8753-961b845b539a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-7,-10)$ and the radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399942} {:answer/id #uuid "f27f0122-8daa-5b13-a293-2ff7b998ce73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(0,0)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399943} {:answer/id #uuid "2340cacd-f3c4-5ae7-99ea-d36258840812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399944} {:answer/id #uuid "3f33726c-a4cf-5d51-a84c-d3798a16d83e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(-7,-10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399945} {:answer/id #uuid "a0981346-e334-5ecc-a493-0c31ebc3ef03" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $100$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399946}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2340cacd-f3c4-5ae7-99ea-d36258840812" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "The center is $(7,10)$ and the radius is $10$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399944} :answer-field/id #uuid "62169293-0e81-54fc-944c-cda58edb5a92" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186399941}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "064ec2a1-8603-5d8c-96f4-94b94ae469b9" :question/math-academy-id "q-117086" :question/problem "What is the center and the radius of the circle with equation $(x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2}=100?$" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is \n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nLet's compare the general equation to our equation side-by-side as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & =100 \\\\ (x-7)^{2}+(y-10)^{2} & ={10}^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that $a=7,$ $b=10,$ and $r=10.$ \n\nTherefore, the circle is centered at $(7,10)$ and its radius is $10.$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253304 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087768 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "3520d323-c6a4-5bce-bac1-1f4c02bd0068" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Center and a Point on the Circle"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1b0c7c14-a555-5e01-8838-765e944ceedf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250784} {:answer/id #uuid "78dc7686-f3de-5b7d-8046-a89585820e9c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251556} {:answer/id #uuid "994030d6-5bdf-505c-ac30-a525c985caa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251870} {:answer/id #uuid "a7739a17-e686-57c5-ba6c-a87d9d4e8077" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=3\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251995} {:answer/id #uuid "d0408c11-e9e7-55cb-940f-15a1df96ac67" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-4)^{2}+(y-3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252393}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "994030d6-5bdf-505c-ac30-a525c985caa5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2}=18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251870} :answer-field/id #uuid "e0900e01-a03b-5ddb-af66-ba4873931f4b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186253187}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "4be1d8bd-eb38-5bfc-b4eb-dd764bc3beed" :question/math-academy-id "q-117096" :question/problem "![](images/16/16d6786a4b1934ed234d4bf0896187aa6e93ec70cf045ddf4b743b1f51eaac2f.png)\n\nThe circle above is centered at $C(-4,-3)$ and the point $X(-1,0)$ lies on the circumference. Find the equation of the circle." :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nThe length of the radius is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CX & =\\sqrt{(-1-(-4))^{2}+(0-(-3))^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{3}^{2}+{3}^{2}} \\\\  & =3\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, our circle is generated by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-(-4))^{2}+(y-(-3))^{2} & ={(3\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x+4)^{2}+(y+3)^{2} & =18\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253306 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d30c4f2-1c9b-56aa-b62b-7e9a63a5c394" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250936} {:answer/id #uuid "51ebda4a-c6ab-56ec-a85d-515c28547d71" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251224} {:answer/id #uuid "9cde4a0d-d36b-53dd-9c07-256ac68ea24e" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251906} {:answer/id #uuid "c3b65520-eb87-5289-bc62-41aa3b67fb30" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y+2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252285} {:answer/id #uuid "df53c346-071e-5d55-b02f-a149afdcd833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "df53c346-071e-5d55-b02f-a149afdcd833" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2}=4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252522} :answer-field/id #uuid "311dd4be-59af-5907-99cb-162e30c5bc61" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252890}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "93ab0f69-1e36-5855-80b5-7cee6cddd602" :question/math-academy-id "q-117102" :question/problem "![](images/af/afd2f435a60fbb5a0f0f83c5f8965a74ca107d1ed4b14d03401f7966a323d2f1.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(2,4)$ and $(2,0)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(2,4)$ and $Y(2,0),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(2-2)^{2}+(4-0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{0}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16} \\\\  & =4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{XY}{2}=\\frac{4}{2}=2.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, we can find the center using the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{2+2}{2},\\frac{4+0}{2})=(2,2)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2$ and center $(a,b)=(2,2),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & ={2}^{2} \\\\ (x-2)^{2}+(y-2)^{2} & =4\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186253310 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087657 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "47863922-b0d5-5a0b-8a01-ffefe3b3c929" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Equation of a Circle Given the Endpoints of a Diameter"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "34b1554c-96e1-5f34-bd7d-39439e7d2d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250994} {:answer/id #uuid "3e0c96c8-b6f3-508c-bbce-383fbffc5d73" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251069} {:answer/id #uuid "71463607-983f-5491-bdcc-71080d1290aa" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=32" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251480} {:answer/id #uuid "78ba35b2-ca4d-559a-9e58-c33761c27a13" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186251553} {:answer/id #uuid "dbfbf876-ab7e-5bb9-b30b-9654f0019146" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x+1)^{2}+(y-1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252487}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "34b1554c-96e1-5f34-bd7d-39439e7d2d90" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2}=8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186250994} :answer-field/id #uuid "233384c8-214c-54f0-a58a-ee2651d7fa9d" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186252869}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "b6f2966b-20a6-5c34-af5a-1e6c31f128aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-117107" :question/problem "![](images/7f/7f1573d17cb9a603727b644da6598355875b0be4b8c43a382e562155cb7a095c.png)\n\nThe line segment $\\overset{―}{XY}$ is a diameter of a circle. Given that $X$ and $Y$ have coordinates $(-1,-3)$ and $(3,1)$, respectively, what is the equation of the circle?" :question/worked-solution "The general equation of a circle with radius $r$ centered at the point $(a,b)$ is\n\n$$\n(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2}={r}^{2}.\n$$\n\nUsing the distance formula to compute the distance between the points $X(-1,-3)$ and $Y(3,1),$ we find that the length of the diameter is \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}XY & =\\sqrt{(-1-3)^{2}+(-3-1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-4)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16\\cdot 2} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the radius of the circle is \n\n$$\nr=\\frac{4\\sqrt{2}}{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.\n$$\n\nSince the center of a circle is the midpoint of the diameter, to find the center we use the midpoint formula as follows:\n\n$$\n(\\frac{{x}_{1}+{x}_{2}}{2},\\frac{{y}_{1}+{y}_{2}}{2})=(\\frac{-1+3}{2},\\frac{-3+1}{2})=(1,-1)\n$$\n\nSo our circle has radius $r=2\\sqrt{2}$ and center $(a,b)=(1,-1),$ and therefore it is represented by the following equation:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-a)^{2}+(y-b)^{2} & ={r}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y-(-1))^{2} & ={(2\\sqrt{2})}^{2} \\\\ (x-1)^{2}+(y+1)^{2} & =8\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186386848 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186110572 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "00a8fb88-4b07-57be-94c5-a6b499c9df5b" :knowledge-point/title "Graphing the Inverse Cosine Function"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2d5cba36-012b-5957-8190-a7b8da7eeb75" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/dd/dd9a1f85153e86fcf69280d8a854e3b47725971f18a214851e38a921856e2319.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386850} {:answer/id #uuid "8c723afa-6aad-5050-9faf-d2048f325a44" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/d6/d6884a96c12d54a728c4ac13ca83a70320f5e61eee6e6df52df181444c246d31.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386851} {:answer/id #uuid "73d37641-965d-529b-b7b4-f470f701b7dd" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/9d/9dcc5a116c2a564547283783a7df7b1cd3a9ab3b76ac24dc2695c4cb367796d5.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386852} {:answer/id #uuid "92b66d8a-8307-509a-b33a-c150b2643ec7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/28/28f6e66182e05a31874c4ae5d04926ab132df76b90f6606238ef9aa1f863b7a0.png" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186386853} {:answer/id #uuid "84e10682-126c-572a-8d30-c9b36c75e00c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045497 :db/ident :answer.type/image} :answer/value "images/64/646fdbadd1ed082c7a86a8f248e9dba0a6445f05b94ef2b2962aafd39c528e07.png" :db/id